# The backend a production build talks to. VITE_API_BASE is inlined at BUILD
# time, so a build without it produces a PWA that calls its own origin — and
# Cloudflare Pages answers POST /api/... with 405, which looks like a backend
# fault rather than a missing build variable.
#
# That is exactly what happened on 2026-08-18: the first deploy passed the
# value on the command line, two later rebuilds (icons, favicon) did not, and
# scanning the join QR started returning 405. Keeping it in this file means a
# plain `npm run build` is always correct; vite.config.ts additionally fails
# the build if it is missing.
VITE_API_BASE=https://stockproof-backend.dms-259.workers.dev
